Z||000007||MAT88GT||05-11-2001||12:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Out of curiosity, do you have a preference between your two Fieros?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would have to say my '85 Gt because it was my first Fiero...it isn't in the best shape compared to my '86, but it holds more sentimental value to me.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>be sure to post some pix of your Fieros<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't have any of my Fiero pictures scanned and uploaded yet but I do have a couple of my Mustang...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://a1060.g.akamai.net/f/1060/597/30minutes/www.zing.com/picture/p9d7798e859df8f10fb8030e7bf8d70d2/fe8936e5.jpg"> <BR>At the dragstrip<P> <IMG SRC="http://a1060.g.akamai.net/f/1060/597/30minutes/www.zing.com/picture/padd539214f2cea951768a096d9668652/fe8936e4.jpg"> <BR>And near a good ol' Iowa corn field<P>The Mustang is basically the same looks wise, but I'm in the middle of a 351w swap that will put me in the mid to low 11's.<P>Thanks for a warm welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1988 Mustang Gt 351w/c4 trans, custom 6pt <BR>1985 Fiero Gt some mods<BR>1986 Fiero 2m4 mint condition||||reg||10
